    [Feature][Attention] Port tested FlashMLA integration onto merged PROLOG main (#18742)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Port external FlashMLA decode onto main, using the reviewed v0.30.0
    integration from #18758 at `d1aa5a515` with the required main
    request-state and graph-dispatch adaptations. This revision replays the
    existing 11 PR commits individually onto main `ccaf14ad31`, preserving
    their original authors, author dates, commit messages, co-authors and
    sign-offs, and adds one test/release-note commit.
    
    - Eligible MRv2 MLA decode uses `flash_mla` / `flash_mla_metadata`; real
    prefill remains on FIA. Cache allocation, guarded PROLOG writes and
    reads use the matching token-fused KV layout.
    - Ordinary DCP decode reads full rank-local KV in one call. Speculative
    causal decode retains history/current attention and exchange/combine.
    Current KV/Q staging precedes the auxiliary-stream ready event.
    - The backend owns metadata refresh, captured buffers, request ordering
    and restrictive decode-graph eligibility. The runner retains the parent
    gather result and invokes the conditional FlashMLA helper before derived
    inputs and graph dispatch.
    - Preserve main's removal of obsolete PD prefill reclassification.
    Resolve the PROLOG conflict with main #19213 by using `tile_size=128`,
    independently of writer cache page size, while retaining this
    integration's writer workspace and scatter behavior.
    - Adapt the new main tile-size test fixture to the writer workspace
    interface without removing assertions. Add 16 API-contract combinations
    and the release note fragment required by current repository guidance.
    - CI workflow files have no PR-specific changes. The previous temporary
    E2E shutdown workaround remains reverted.
    
    The query-boundary None guard, generic builder request interface, PD
    layout validation and FP16 writer eligibility remain follow-ups.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Eligible MRv2 configurations select FlashMLA decode, including
    DCP/DSpark and supported PD connectors. PROLOG uses its supported tile
    attribute for non-128 writer pages. This revision does not introduce the
    later BF16-only selection restriction or Mooncake MLA shape guard; PD
    endpoints must use compatible cache layouts and configurations.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ten related CPU test files: **684 passed, 4 existing skips**, using
    CI-pinned vLLM `c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b` and
    `VLLM_VERSION=0.31.0.dev0`.
    - New tile-size regression covers 128/768 writer pages, FlashMLA on/off,
    KV quantization modes 0/1 and query quantization on/off. Against the
    previous PR source, four ordinary-FIA 768-page cases fail and twelve
    pass; the corrected source passes all sixteen. API checks preserve cache
    identities, shapes and slot mappings.
    - Retain all existing PD prompt-tail, graph-gate, dummy-batch, DCP and
    PROLOG assertions, including the new main tile-size regression.
    - Full `bash format.sh ci` and diff whitespace checks passed on this
    candidate.
    - Isolated reproductions of the existing ordinary `git rebase` step pass
    against both adopted main `ccaf14ad31` and observed newer main
    `3abf581d36`. The latter result's complete tree equals a normal merge
    with that main. This replaces the previous snapshot/rebase blocker; it
    is not a claim that all remote CI has passed.
    - The only production-code difference from previous PR head `4231e9cb86`
    is the fixed PROLOG tile attribute and explanatory comment. Original 11
    commit author records and trailers were checked individually after
    replay.
    - No new NPU execution, graph replay, PD E2E, GPQA or performance
    validation was run. Remote results must be assessed on this exact head.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
